    <h1>Does GDPR Apply to US Companies? The Territorial-Scope Test Explained</h1>
    <p class="last-updated">Published September 18, 2026</p>

    <p>Yes, the GDPR can apply to US companies -- even those with no office, server, or employee in Europe. The regulation's reach is determined by whose data you process and what you do with it, not by where your business is incorporated. If your app or website collects personal data from people located in the European Economic Area (EEA), you may be subject to the full weight of the GDPR regardless of your company's size or location.</p>

    <p>This guide breaks down the specific legal triggers in Article 3 of the GDPR, walks through concrete examples a US app developer would recognize, clarifies the situations that do <em>not</em> bring a US company within scope, and explains what compliance actually requires if the regulation does apply to you. If you want a quick answer on which privacy laws cover your specific setup, you can run a <a href="/tools/privacy-law-checker/">privacy law eligibility check based on your platforms and audience</a> in under a minute.</p>

